						<!-- Section: Meet the Team -->
							<section id="team" class="main">
                <div class="content main">
                  <header class="major content">
                    <h2>About Magick Data Sciences</h2>
                  </header>
                    <p>
                      Magick's origin story revolves around a central tenant: a shared love of helping others solve problems. Some people have a passion for sports, playing poker, or cultivating rare orchids. We do too, but generally not as much as we like digging into a new data set, optimizing a costly legacy business process, or discovering a new way to make complex information accessible to anyone.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                      So we packed up our corporate bag of tricks, donned our enchanted robes, and set out into the World with the mission of turning our experience and curiosity into quality of life improvements for people who spend their days toiling with the oft-forgotten and overlooked parts of business&mdash;spreadsheets, databases, back office tools.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                      Along the way we've encountered like-minded people who know how to discover, document, design, and engineer unique solutions for our clients, in ways which can only be described as <em>magickal<em>.
                    </p>
                    <hr/>
                    <h3><strong>Meet the Founders</strong></h3>
                  <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-6 col-12-medium">
                      <h4 class="center-align">Vas Paruchuri</h4>
                      <p>As a data scientist, portfolio manager, and developer, Vas focuses on generating practical business solutions from complex data sets. He has an interdisciplinary background spanning theoretical physics to finance to software development. Vas has an easy approach to breaking down problems and communicating solutions in a plain-spoken manner.</p>
                      <p>In his free time, Vas enjoys teaching young people how to enjoy solving problems and become life long learners.</p>
                      <p>Vas has a B.S.E. from Cornell University in Applied Physics and a Ph.D. from Harvard University in Physics.</p>
                      <ul class="icons">
                        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vas-paruchuri-65aa0b21" class="icon brands fa-linkedin"><span class="label">LinkedIn</span></a></li>
                        <li><a href="https://github.com/chester333" class="icon brands fa-github"><span class="label">GitHub</span></a></li>
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-6 col-12-medium">
                      <h4>Ben Rossi</h4>
                      <p>Ben is an information artist, UX developer, product evangelist, and problem solver with over 20 years of practical experience and endless curiousity. With a background in design and software development for complex systems, Ben has achieved recognized success in large, multinational organizations, as well as small start-up environments across a diverse set of industries.</p>
                      <p>When he's not untangling (usually undocumented) internal processes, crafting engaging experiences, or proposing novel solutions for business challenges, Ben can be found in his workshop.</p>
                      <p>Ben has a B.A. Art and Visual Technology from George Mason University.</p>
                      <ul class="icons">
                        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/benrossi/" class="icon brands fa-linkedin"><span class="label">LinkedIn</span></a></li>
                        <li><a href="https://twitter.com/b_rossi" class="icon brands fa-twitter"><span class="label">Twitter</span></a></li>
                        <li><a href="https://github.com/brossi" class="icon brands fa-github"><span class="label">GitHub</span></a></li>
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
							</section>
					</div>

          <div class="row">
          <section id="contact" class="main special">
            <div class="col-6">
            <header class="minor">
              <h2>Let's get started!</h2>
              <h4>conjure@magickdata.io</h4>
            </header>

            <blockquote class="prophecy" citation="Ancient Prophecy of Caerbannog">It shall be then, when spreadsheet values no longer match their assigned column type, and the deadline is nigh, a faithful daemon will carry a petition for assistance to those strong in the Magick. For once they appear, the problem will be solved. And there will be much rejoicing.</blockquote>

            <form name="submit-to-google-sheet">
              <div class="row gtr-uniform">
                <div class="col-6 col-12-xsmall">
                  <input name="name" type="text" placeholder="Your Name" required>
                </div>
                <div class="col-6 col-12-xsmall">
                  <input name="email" type="email" placeholder="Email" required>
                </div>
              </div>

                <div class="col-12">
                  <textarea name="message" placeholder="What can we help you with?" rows="6"></textarea>
                </div>
                <div class="col-12">
                  <ul class="actions">
                    <li><button type="submit">Unlease the daemon!</button></li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>
            </form>

          </section>
